  "query_preview": "..\nLatest Update: 0615Z\n\nThe upper ridge will be about the same strength tomorrow, and then\nincrease in intensity on Friday before a trough moves in for\nSaturday. There is potential for scattered fire weather \nconditions on Friday since well above average temperatures will\noccur.\n\nMostly dry conditions on Saturday morning are expected to be\nreplaced by rain showers as a cold front moves through. A tenth \nto a quarter inch of accumulation is expected south of the \nMissouri River, and mainly less than a quarter inch north of the \nriver through Monday evening. The Little Rockies has up to an inch\nof snow possible on grass and tree limbs through Monday evening.\nOther locations have mostly a trace expected in that time (less\nthan one inch). A decent dusting may be a great opportunity for\npictures, especially on Monday afternoon in the west if clouds\nclear out a bit.\n\nAlthough there is some uncertainty beyond Monday, weak troughing\nappears as though it will remain in place to bring chances for\nprecipitation again in the middle of the week. This is according\nto the GFS ensemble anyway.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nIncreased winds on day 1 and 2 in the afternoons and decreased\nRelative humidity on Friday afternoon.\n\nThere is moderate confidence on both winds being within +/- 8 \nknots of the forecast, and precipitation amounts through Monday.",
